  body: "# Earnings assessment: weekly amount and timing facts\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation;
    unreviewed. No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured guidance requires identification
    of the benefit week and weekly earnings amount, and distinguishes earnings already in payment, newly
    payable earnings and changed earnings.\n\n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 86007–86008, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/698462dd468d351e1406b4a7/dmgch86.pdf#page=4)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `909d328088dda0b6a94e0fc671bfa41f6d300689ff02d6f8a0292e30172f9908`.\n\
    \nThis identifies facts the guidance requires, not the effective date for a claimant. Adjacent rules,
    changes during an AIP and decision-making law remain relevant.\n\nThe capture date, the publication
    page's update date and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and
    memos need their own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/earnings
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The two paragraphs explicitly connect earnings assessment to benefit-week timing and
      the state of the earnings stream.
    evidence:
    - page: page/86/0004
      quote: "86007 Earnings are taken into account in SPC in the same way as any other income. The DM
        will need to\nestablish\n\n\n1. the first day of the benefit week from which the earnings should
        be taken into account and\n\n\n2. the weekly amount.\n\n\nThe date from which earnings are taken
        into account\n86008 The date from which the weekly amount of a claimant’s net earnings are taken
        into account\ndepends upon whether\n\n\n1. there are already regular earnings in payment\n\n\n\
        \      1.1 at the date of claim for SPC or\n\n\n      1.2 following the end of an AIP or\n\n\n\
        2. earnings become payable whilst SPC is in payment or\n\n\n3. the amount of existing earnings
        changes."
      locator: DMG 86007–86008
  - target: term/pc-benefit-week
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The two paragraphs explicitly connect earnings assessment to benefit-week timing and
      the state of the earnings stream.
    evidence:
